.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH 1seed 1  "1seed 0.8.1" 
.SH NAME
1seed \- Deterministic cryptographic keys from a single seed
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB1seed\fR [\fB\-\-seed\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-realm\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deterministic cryptographic keys from a single seed
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\-file\fR \fI<SEED_FILE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-realm\fR \fI<REALM>\fR

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBSEED_REALM\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
1seed\-age(1)
Age encryption keys and operations
.TP
1seed\-ssh(1)
SSH keys and operations
.TP
1seed\-sign(1)
Ed25519 signing keys and operations
.TP
1seed\-derive(1)
Derive passwords, mnemonics, and raw bytes
.TP
1seed\-init(1)
Initialize: store seed in OS keychain (~/.1seed on Linux)
.TP
1seed\-forget(1)
Remove seed from OS keychain and ~/.1seed
.TP
1seed\-status(1)
Show status and derived keys
.TP
1seed\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
    1seed init \-\-generate            Create and store a seed
    1seed age pub                    Show age public key
    1seed \-\-realm work ssh add       Add work SSH key to agent
    echo secret | 1seed age encrypt  Encrypt to self
    1seed derive password github.com Derive password

FLAGS / ENVIRONMENT:
    \-\-seed\-file          Seed file path (takes precedence over SEED_FILE)
    SEED_NO_KEYRING      Use ~/.1seed only (bypass keyring)
    \-\-realm              Default realm (takes precedence over SEED_REALM)

STORAGE:
    Priority: flag > env > keyring > ~/.1seed
    Keyring: macOS Keychain, Windows Credential Manager
    Linux: init stores the seed in ~/.1seed (mode 0600)
.SH VERSION
v0.8.1
